From 580d9b6625bd7bf33679381ae17b445113f987f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:25:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Read Member Voting History PDFs with native Julia code

getSession57HouseLegislativeMemberVotingHistory no longer needs Java
(JavaCall and Tabula) or the 7z program (p7zip_jll), so it no longer
needs JULIA_COPY_STACKS=1 either. The zip is read by the new ZipReader
module and the PDFs by the new PDFText module, both pure Julia; the only
new dependency is Inflate.jl, a pure-Julia zlib/Deflate decompressor.

The output for the 57th Legislature, 2nd Regular Session is identical
to the old version's: all 67,945 votes, every column. A first call in a
Julia session takes about 30 s instead of about 90 s, and a second call
about 15 s.

- src/PDFText.jl: reads a PDF's text as lines of words with positions
- src/ZipReader.jl: reads the files in a zip, checking their CRC-32
- test/readers.jl: offline tests of both, run from test/runtests.jl

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019awDnsGJAcXbzPNQg6VhqU
